## Prioritizing Content Ideas

Score each idea on four factors:

### 1. Customer Impact (40%)
Frequency in research; percentage of customers facing the challenge; emotional charge of the pain point; potential LTV of customers with this need.

### 2. Content-Market Fit (30%)
Alignment with problems your product solves; unique insights from customer research; supporting customer stories; natural path to product interest.

### 3. Search Potential (20%)
Monthly search volume; competitiveness; related long-tail opportunities; growing vs. declining interest.

### 4. Resource Requirements (10%)
Expertise to create authoritative content; additional research needed; assets required (graphics, data, examples).

### Scoring Template

| Idea | Customer Impact (40%) | Content-Market Fit (30%) | Search Potential (20%) | Resources (10%) | Total |
|------|----------------------|-------------------------|----------------------|-----------------|-------|
| Topic A | 8 | 9 | 7 | 6 | 8.0 |
| Topic B | 6 | 7 | 9 | 8 | 7.1 |

---

## Output Format

### 1. Content Pillars
3-5 pillars with rationale, subtopic clusters for each, and how pillars connect to product.

### 2. Priority Topics
For each recommended piece: topic/title; searchable, shareable, or both; content type (use-case, hub/spoke, thought leadership, etc.); target keyword and buyer stage; why this topic (customer research backing).

### 3. Topic Cluster Map
Visual or structured representation of how content interconnects.

